<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert Einstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert Einstein was a German-born physicist, born in Ulm, whose theories of special and general relativity transformed physics. In 1905, while working at the Swiss patent office in Bern, he published papers on relativity, light quanta and Brownian motion, and he received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Physics for 1921. Of Jewish origin, he left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1933 and settled in Princeton in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-einstein.jpg" alt="Albert Einstein" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oren Jack Turner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_Einstein_Head_cleaned.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
